# Add support for AF_UNIX sockets (followup)
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/7650 state=opened
# Follow-up of !2786, which appears to have been abandoned.

Depends on !8182, !8575, !8578, !8863, !9831, !9835

# What is supported
- basic socket operations (socket, listen, bind, connect, accept, getsockname, ioctlsocket, send, recv, sendto, recvfrom,  WSAIoctl(SIO_AF_UNIX_GETPEERPID))

# Was is not supported 
- abstract sockets
- ConnectEx
- DGRAM
- WSAIoctl(SIO_AF_UNIX_SETBINDPARENTPATH)
- WSAIoctl( SIO_AF_UNIX_SETCONNPARENTPATH)

# Why was the chdir() design chosen?
The path specified with the `bind()` function on Windows is converted to a Unix path within Wine. If this path is longer than the maximum path length allowed by the `bind()` call, a `chdir` command is executed to that path, and the filename in the current directory is used. Since this happens within `wineserver`, it has no effect on the calling Windows application.

# Related issues
- [Bug 60201](https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=60201) - Implement `SIO_AF_UNIX_GETPEERPID` ioctl 
- [Bug 52568](https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=52568) - Support for `AF_UNIX` is missing
- [DBus](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/dbus/dbus/-/merge_requests/249) - Add Unix socket support on Windows 
- [Bug 60887](https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=60887) - Opening files or AF_UNIX sockets via Volume GUID paths (\\?\Volume{GUID}\...) fails with ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND
- [Bug 60888](https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=60888) - DefineDosDeviceW mapping a drive letter to a subdirectory succeeds, but accessing files via that drive letter fails with ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND
# Related applications
- [Kontakt 7](https://appdb.winehq.org/objectManager.php?sClass=application&iId=2123)

# Execute minimal test case

1. checkout wine
```
cd ~
mkdir src
git clone git@gitlab.winehq.org:rhabacker/wine.git
cd wine
```
2. Optional: In dlls/ws2_32/tests/sock.c wrap all calls to test functions after `Init()` until `test_afunix()` and after with #if 0 ... #endif to reduce the number of unrelated messages

